Viewer token and channel for this box's own page only (audit 2026-10-13, A2).

receiver-access.js put the viewer token into localStorage of whatever page loaded it, and any site could load
it with a script tag; the WebSocket only compared the token. On the F50 a request with Origin
https://evil.example got the script (200, with the token) and the channel (101). The box now writes
receiver-access.json (run-receiver.py), which the receiver serves only to its own page (no Origin or the
box's own address, Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin or none; Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy same-origin, no-store);
the page reads it before starting. The WebSocket and POST /api/display refuse other origins as well.
After the change on the F50: the token file 403 from another site (fetch or script), the channel closed with
"invalid token" before any message; the box's page still gets the token and plays.

